"total":-3.5},"snow_normal":2.7},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, 1 daily record low","records":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","change":"Memphis' nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","rain":"Memphis has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 52\u00b0F was the 27th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 151 since 1875, the coolest since 2022.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 81% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>52\u00b0F</strong> was the 27th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 151 since 1875, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 63\u00b0F, and the record is 85\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>37\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Memphis' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Memphis has set <strong class=\"sig\">25 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 65 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">125 record highs</strong>, far more than the 65 that chance alone would give. The 1950s hold the most record highs of any decade (51). Memphis' all-time high is 108\u00b0F, on July 13, 1980.","t_chg":"Memphis' nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 151 complete years: Memphis' average low shows no clear change: +0.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.10) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Memphis' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.25\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.20 to +0.29), about +3.7\u00b0F since 1875. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.52\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.22 to +0.82) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Memphis has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Memphis' yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.51 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +0.86), about +7.8 inches since 1872. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 54.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1957 (76.85 in); the driest, 1916 (33.44 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}